WEBVTT

00:06.047 --> 00:08.049
[opening theme music playing]

00:31.114 --> 00:33.950
THE TRUNK

00:34.034 --> 00:36.244
[ominous music playing]

00:36.327 --> 00:38.329
[loud rattling]

00:39.205 --> 00:40.874
[thunder rumbling]

00:42.083 --> 00:45.420
[phone buzzing]

00:47.672 --> 00:49.674
[thunder rumbling]

00:51.760 --> 00:53.011
[phone buzzing]

00:53.845 --> 00:55.138
[phone line ringing]

01:01.352 --> 01:03.772
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed cannot be reached.

01:03.855 --> 01:06.107
At the tone, please record your message.

01:06.191 --> 01:07.317
[disconnect tone]

01:07.817 --> 01:08.818
[keys rattle]

01:08.902 --> 01:11.863
You could invent a decent excuse
before you go to his house!

01:12.906 --> 01:14.157
You can't just burst in there.

01:15.033 --> 01:15.867
Move now.

01:16.993 --> 01:19.329
I don't have time to argue
with a fake husband.

01:26.836 --> 01:27.670
[door slams]

01:37.263 --> 01:39.265
[thunder rumbling]

01:53.404 --> 01:55.406
[gentle piano music playing]

02:02.080 --> 02:03.790
[thunder rumbling]

02:13.091 --> 02:15.093
[gentle piano music continues]

02:17.971 --> 02:19.180
[woman breathes heavily]

02:24.477 --> 02:26.646
[sniffling]

02:31.442 --> 02:33.444
- [siren wailing]
- [panting]

02:48.668 --> 02:50.587
[thunder rumbling]

02:50.670 --> 02:52.672
[gentle piano music continues]

03:14.402 --> 03:15.695
[music fades]

03:16.362 --> 03:18.364
- [thunder rumbles]
- [door closes]

03:39.427 --> 03:40.637
Go ahead, say it.

03:41.179 --> 03:43.056
This better be a confession.

03:44.933 --> 03:46.392
What did In-ji say?

03:48.811 --> 03:51.147
That I had cameras inserted into it?

03:53.942 --> 03:55.276
Well, yes, that's true.

03:56.194 --> 03:58.571
Sorry. I didn't know it was a crime
to observe you like that.

04:00.490 --> 04:02.533
I had no choice. I was going crazy.

04:02.617 --> 04:04.452
Look, I wanted us to get back together.

04:04.535 --> 04:06.704
I just needed to see you yearning,
you know?

04:08.164 --> 04:10.875
Still longing for me,
even when In-ji was around you.

04:17.715 --> 04:19.425
Are you saying you did this so

04:20.510 --> 04:22.220
you and I could be together again?

04:23.805 --> 04:26.933
You told the doctors
to save the child's life, knowing I'd die,

04:28.351 --> 04:30.395
as I was getting wheeled into the OR.

04:32.355 --> 04:34.023
How could you do that to me?

04:34.899 --> 04:36.818
How could sweet Jeong-won do that?

04:38.319 --> 04:40.405
When you walked into the street that day,

04:41.864 --> 04:43.992
I blamed you and wanted you to know.

04:46.703 --> 04:48.204
I felt horrible

04:49.372 --> 04:50.581
for our child.

04:55.795 --> 04:57.463
All I wanted was to die with it.

04:58.631 --> 05:01.801
After I got pregnant,
every goddamn day, every second, was hell.

05:02.969 --> 05:05.930
It felt like I was suddenly the most
useless person in the whole world.

05:06.806 --> 05:07.724
I was withering away

05:07.807 --> 05:10.560
because I dreaded having to give birth
to that child more than death.

05:10.643 --> 05:11.769
But you… [sobs softly]

05:12.854 --> 05:13.813
…you were just excited.

05:13.896 --> 05:16.733
It was giving you
some new sense of purpose. [sniffles]

05:17.317 --> 05:18.651
All of a sudden, I was

05:18.735 --> 05:21.696
some limp appendage
carrying your child, nothing more.

05:21.779 --> 05:22.989
Do you know what that's like?

05:23.072 --> 05:25.366
Then why didn't you just say it, huh?!

05:25.450 --> 05:27.702
You should've told me
you weren't cut out for it!

05:27.785 --> 05:30.913
And I always would've been haunted
seeing how disappointed you were.

05:32.206 --> 05:34.959
Moms are only supposed to ask them
to save the child first, right?

05:36.002 --> 05:37.795
And I hated myself then too.

05:40.256 --> 05:42.842
Soon, I wanted
anything maternal in me to die.

05:53.478 --> 05:56.898
I blamed myself for not understanding
how you were feeling back then.

05:58.441 --> 06:01.235
I thought I was being
a total self-involved idiot.

06:02.028 --> 06:03.154
That's how I dealt with this.

06:04.113 --> 06:05.615
And I thought all of it would go away

06:05.698 --> 06:08.159
if you and I could be together
like we used to.

06:09.786 --> 06:11.245
But how could you

06:12.497 --> 06:14.374
do what my father did to us?

06:16.751 --> 06:18.711
I was scared. I didn't know what to do.

06:21.172 --> 06:24.258
I didn't have the same kind
of power over you that I used to.

06:25.760 --> 06:26.844
Jeong-won,

06:28.304 --> 06:29.972
we're still accomplices, right?

06:31.516 --> 06:34.852
I killed our child,
and you killed your mother, didn't you?

06:36.104 --> 06:39.107
Since we've both done awful things,
maybe we can atone together.

06:39.690 --> 06:41.442
The two of us. Hmm?

06:51.661 --> 06:53.329
You're demented, Seo-yeon.

06:54.747 --> 06:56.082
I'm going to atone.

06:58.376 --> 07:00.795
Just not by your side.
That's over for good now.

07:13.266 --> 07:15.268
[thunder rumbling]

07:19.814 --> 07:20.940
[door opens]

07:21.899 --> 07:23.151
- [sobs]
- [door closes]

07:29.115 --> 07:30.241
[whimpers]

07:31.576 --> 07:33.578
[crying]

07:36.789 --> 07:38.416
[somber piano music playing]

07:38.499 --> 07:40.501
[crying continues]

07:42.253 --> 07:44.547
[somber piano music continues]

08:26.964 --> 08:28.382
You wanna get out of the city?

08:38.851 --> 08:40.853
[somber piano music continues]

08:53.950 --> 08:55.952
[somber piano music continues]

08:57.411 --> 08:58.454
[gasps]

08:59.413 --> 09:01.666
[thunder rumbling]

09:02.583 --> 09:03.584
[gasps]

09:05.378 --> 09:07.380
[somber piano music continues]

09:16.138 --> 09:17.723
[music fades]

09:20.893 --> 09:23.187
[footsteps approaching]

09:34.699 --> 09:37.868
I'm sure you knew there were cameras.
Why'd you stay quiet?

09:40.955 --> 09:43.291
Well, I mean,
I didn't know how to break it to you.

09:44.208 --> 09:46.711
I should have taken care of it.
I didn't want you to know.

09:48.671 --> 09:50.548
I'm sorry I kept this from you.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.758
I'm tired of excuses.

09:53.926 --> 09:55.511
You turned a blind eye to the whole thing

09:55.595 --> 09:57.513
'cause you didn't want
trouble in the marriage.

09:58.222 --> 10:00.141
You should know I didn't shrug it off.

10:01.726 --> 10:04.979
I actually grabbed Seo-yeon by her hair
and roughed her up a little.

10:05.813 --> 10:07.690
Really? You… you hit Seo-yeon?

10:08.316 --> 10:09.275
I clobbered her.

10:10.484 --> 10:12.653
Those blue pills taped to the record…

10:13.613 --> 10:15.531
When I found out what they were, I…

10:16.324 --> 10:18.534
I pretty much went
berserk on her, you know?

10:19.702 --> 10:22.663
If I wanted to, I could've broken
two or three of her ribs, so you know.

10:23.748 --> 10:25.958
Jujitsu pays off, as it turns out.

10:28.419 --> 10:29.920
Man, I wish I'd seen that.

10:31.631 --> 10:33.257
You might've had to take a side.

10:35.343 --> 10:37.345
[romantic piano music playing]

10:55.905 --> 10:57.823
[chuckles]

10:58.699 --> 11:00.159
You actually attacked Seo-yeon?

11:02.203 --> 11:04.997
[laughs] Crazy. You pulled her hair
and punched her.

11:05.081 --> 11:06.666
[both laughing]

11:09.627 --> 11:11.629
[romantic piano music continues]

11:32.525 --> 11:34.068
[Jeong-won] It's a whole family.

11:45.329 --> 11:47.123
I wanna go get some groceries.

11:47.915 --> 11:50.835
We should get a little banchan
and a few cold ones.

11:50.918 --> 11:52.586
We'll banter together as we go.

11:53.546 --> 11:55.047
We'll be like, "Do we need all this?"

11:55.131 --> 11:57.717
Or, "Let's not do ground coffee.
Whole bean's good."

12:01.387 --> 12:02.805
Do you have a favorite dish?

12:06.392 --> 12:07.810
Would you mind if I cooked?

12:14.692 --> 12:15.776
[music fades]

12:15.860 --> 12:17.737
How long are you gonna be
living in that house?

12:20.489 --> 12:21.615
If I were you…

12:28.205 --> 12:29.039
Let's go.

12:37.298 --> 12:38.507
What was that, huh?

12:38.591 --> 12:40.426
"If I were you…" You'd what?

12:42.511 --> 12:44.388
[chuckles] You know,
you shouldn't do that.

12:44.472 --> 12:46.307
- Stop yourself like that.
- [laughs]

12:46.390 --> 12:47.850
[melodic piano music playing]

12:47.933 --> 12:49.018
- Mm.
- What is it?

12:51.395 --> 12:52.313
What is it, huh?

12:52.396 --> 12:54.398
[melodic piano music continues]

13:05.785 --> 13:06.827
[In-ji chuckles]

13:06.911 --> 13:09.121
♪ You don't have to stay ♪

13:09.205 --> 13:11.499
♪ Just let the past decay ♪

13:11.582 --> 13:15.002
♪ 'Cause I know it's not your fault ♪

13:16.420 --> 13:19.381
♪ You think you're not enough ♪

13:19.465 --> 13:22.426
♪ But I know we'll make it through ♪

13:22.510 --> 13:25.387
♪ Just escape from the darkness ♪

13:27.223 --> 13:29.391
♪ I won't let you drown ♪

13:29.475 --> 13:32.353
♪ I can pull you out of shadows ♪

13:32.436 --> 13:36.023
♪ Just hold my hand, and we'll be fine ♪

13:36.565 --> 13:38.192
♪ Turn around ♪

13:38.734 --> 13:39.985
♪ Oh ♪

13:40.069 --> 13:44.073
♪ Baby, I'll be your savior ♪

13:48.828 --> 13:50.746
♪ What if we die? ♪

13:51.372 --> 13:56.585
♪ We cannot be happy
If there's nothing to lose ♪

13:58.963 --> 14:00.965
♪ What if we try ♪

14:01.507 --> 14:02.800
♪ To stay alive? ♪

14:02.883 --> 14:06.345
♪ Will we ever be free from the past? ♪

14:06.846 --> 14:09.265
♪ What do we live for? ♪

14:10.349 --> 14:11.475
♪ Mm-mm ♪

14:11.976 --> 14:14.937
♪ What do we live for? ♪

14:17.022 --> 14:19.316
♪ What do we live for? ♪

14:19.942 --> 14:21.777
♪ Mm-mm-mm ♪

14:21.861 --> 14:24.697
♪ So what do we live for? ♪

14:27.366 --> 14:29.368
[music fades]

14:36.166 --> 14:38.419
No, keep your hand there.
I'll warm it for you.

14:42.423 --> 14:44.383
I was sure about you from day one.

14:46.886 --> 14:48.554
[In-ji] Han Jeong-won is my husband.

14:55.185 --> 14:56.604
[camera shutter clicks]

14:56.687 --> 14:59.064
[photographer] All right.
Look this way, please.

14:59.148 --> 15:01.066
One, two…

15:01.150 --> 15:02.526
[camera shutter clicks]

15:02.610 --> 15:05.988
[Jeong-won] The mausoleum,
the graduation ceremony…

15:07.698 --> 15:09.783
That was a pretty rough day, honestly.

15:11.452 --> 15:13.704
I felt like you were the only one
who could understand

15:13.787 --> 15:15.372
what I had been going through.

15:16.874 --> 15:19.001
If I had gotten to know you in those days…

15:21.837 --> 15:24.632
if we'd met back then,
how would it have turned out?

15:25.841 --> 15:27.134
[Jeong-won sighs]

15:27.217 --> 15:28.344
[wistful music playing]

15:28.427 --> 15:31.347
We might've broken up
or drifted apart quickly.

15:31.430 --> 15:32.723
I mean, who knows.

15:33.766 --> 15:34.642
I just…

15:38.520 --> 15:40.397
I'm almost certain
I would've recognized you

15:40.481 --> 15:42.608
even if we saw each other here and there.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.409
I feel something strong here.

15:53.577 --> 15:55.162
And I know I wanna be with you.

16:11.303 --> 16:12.346
[sighs]

16:13.931 --> 16:15.307
I want a divorce.

16:19.561 --> 16:21.647
We're here 'cause I wanted to end things.

16:24.525 --> 16:27.695
Did I do… something wrong?

16:27.778 --> 16:29.863
Is there an actual problem here?

16:31.782 --> 16:33.867
Jeong-won, this marriage is a failure.

16:35.828 --> 16:37.955
And it's my fault. I crossed a boundary.

16:38.914 --> 16:40.207
At this point, I don't…

16:40.749 --> 16:43.293
I don't have a reason
to keep our relationship going,

16:43.377 --> 16:44.378
so I should

16:45.546 --> 16:46.714
stop it right now.

16:48.340 --> 16:49.383
[scoffs]

16:51.844 --> 16:53.470
It's time to be real, okay?

16:54.054 --> 16:57.850
Acting all cold and aloof…
bringing up the manual.

16:58.392 --> 17:02.146
It's a lie 'cause deep down, you're
desperate for something to hold onto.

17:03.313 --> 17:04.857
Haven't you been marrying yourself off

17:04.940 --> 17:07.943
because you… you couldn't survive
being alone for much longer?

17:08.027 --> 17:10.237
We're both
incredibly fragile human beings.

17:10.320 --> 17:11.947
That's why our lives are a mess.

17:12.448 --> 17:15.242
So, for once, would you stop talking
about boundaries and just…

17:20.622 --> 17:22.416
just admit it to me, will you?

17:26.503 --> 17:28.839
Just say it. You're falling for me too.

17:40.934 --> 17:42.853
I told you I stepped over the line.

17:43.937 --> 17:47.691
Sorry that doesn't mean you have become
a significant person in my life.

17:54.823 --> 17:56.867
It's over. Do you understand, Jeong-won?

18:04.083 --> 18:06.085
[wind whistling]

18:12.132 --> 18:14.051
[melodic acoustic guitar music playing]

18:23.852 --> 18:24.937
[device beeps]

18:27.106 --> 18:29.191
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

18:33.237 --> 18:36.198
[Jeong-won] If we'd met back then,
how would it have turned out?

18:37.407 --> 18:39.576
If I had gotten to know you in those days…

18:41.161 --> 18:43.038
I'm almost certain
I would've recognized you

18:43.122 --> 18:45.165
even if we saw each other here and there.

18:45.791 --> 18:47.543
[Seo-yeon] Although, for a low-rent whore,

18:47.626 --> 18:51.088
you really have an amazing ability
to bring bad luck to everyone around.

18:52.297 --> 18:55.634
[Tae-seong] Would you give me attention,
In-ji, if I murdered Jeong-won?

18:55.717 --> 18:57.261
[Seo-yeon] Why bullshit Jeong-won?

18:57.761 --> 19:00.639
[In-ji] Don't get me wrong.
I'm not hesitating out of respect for you.

19:00.722 --> 19:03.225
[Seo-yeon] I guess you don't want
Jeong-won to get hurt, do you?

19:04.852 --> 19:06.687
You're a fake. We know it's true.

19:07.688 --> 19:09.773
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

19:29.001 --> 19:32.379
[man] You sure I can just have it?
Why are you giving it up?

19:33.046 --> 19:35.674
Thanks for opening early
on all those mornings so I could go.

19:35.757 --> 19:38.427
Well, I'll see you around soon.
Hopefully, the weather clears up.

19:39.219 --> 19:40.179
Uh, no.

19:41.513 --> 19:42.931
I'll be gone for good.

19:54.693 --> 19:56.236
[music fades]

19:57.988 --> 20:00.449
[Jeong-won] Hey, are you in there?
Open the door, In-ji!

20:01.200 --> 20:02.075
Noh In-ji, you there?

20:03.535 --> 20:04.494
Jesus, quiet!

20:06.413 --> 20:07.664
Mr. Han?

20:11.251 --> 20:12.085
[door lock beeps]

20:13.003 --> 20:14.129
[inhales sharply]

20:14.755 --> 20:15.839
[exhales sharply]

20:17.507 --> 20:18.592
Hold this.

20:22.387 --> 20:23.764
[beeping]

20:24.389 --> 20:25.265
[door lock beeps]

20:27.351 --> 20:28.227
Welcome.

20:34.024 --> 20:35.651
You can keep your shoes on.

20:37.027 --> 20:38.070
[door lock beeps]

20:44.785 --> 20:45.911
[coffee machine beeps]

20:48.622 --> 20:50.207
[coffee pouring]

20:58.674 --> 21:00.342
Oh. Thank you.

21:03.845 --> 21:05.138
Well, you seem normal.

21:07.891 --> 21:10.811
Well, uh, you… don't know me,
so why are you…

21:11.603 --> 21:14.398
Well, I'd guess you're in love with her,
and it's driving you nuts.

21:18.777 --> 21:20.529
Can you tell me where she is?

21:20.612 --> 21:21.905
[chuckles]

21:21.989 --> 21:23.699
You should know. How would I know?

21:24.950 --> 21:26.326
You're married, aren't you?

21:26.410 --> 21:28.870
I'm sure she's off somewhere
worrying about you as we speak.

21:29.746 --> 21:30.747
[inhales sharply]

21:31.748 --> 21:33.000
Look for her yourself.

21:33.500 --> 21:36.003
She's finished
with the guy who owns this flat.

21:38.171 --> 21:40.173
Hmm. I appreciate the drink.

21:58.900 --> 21:59.943
Lovebirds, huh?

22:01.194 --> 22:03.447
- Could we move things a little faster?
- Yes, sir.

22:03.530 --> 22:05.490
And please get rid of
the broken fixture ASAP.

22:05.574 --> 22:06.908
- That's the priority.
- We're on it.

22:06.992 --> 22:08.910
- Okay, thanks. And keep it up.
- Of course.

22:09.870 --> 22:11.371
We need to get this done fast.

22:11.455 --> 22:13.457
[uneasy music playing]

22:15.208 --> 22:16.668
[man 2] Let's get to the glass first.

22:19.921 --> 22:21.923
[uneasy music continues]

22:38.440 --> 22:40.442
[music intensifies]

22:49.951 --> 22:52.454
[man] She said she was done kayaking.
Seemed pretty sure about it.

22:52.537 --> 22:53.830
Even gave me her paddles.

22:55.749 --> 22:59.252
Um, would you just reach out
if you ever see her around here again?

23:02.923 --> 23:03.757
[paper tears]

23:05.300 --> 23:06.385
[man] Sure.

23:12.933 --> 23:13.892
[sighs]

23:21.274 --> 23:22.359
[phone buzzing]

23:23.819 --> 23:24.986
[phone buzzing]

23:26.571 --> 23:28.573
NM LEE SEON

23:30.826 --> 23:31.660
Um, hello?

23:32.160 --> 23:33.453
This is Lee Seon.

23:33.537 --> 23:36.331
The contract you had with us
has been cut short. I'm sorry.

23:36.832 --> 23:38.166
As you may know,

23:38.250 --> 23:40.544
you are entitled to request
financial damages from us

23:40.627 --> 23:41.670
if you'd like to do so.

23:42.421 --> 23:45.048
[Jeong-won] Oh, no. I won't be doing that.

23:46.299 --> 23:48.969
Uh, just make sure
that no harm comes to Ms. Noh.

23:50.387 --> 23:53.223
Yes. We'll see to it, Mr. Han.

23:53.306 --> 23:55.767
Uh… the two of us talked.

23:55.851 --> 23:57.227
Mostly as friends.

23:57.811 --> 23:59.604
I just wish I knew more about her.

23:59.688 --> 24:01.398
If you know where she might be or…

24:03.900 --> 24:05.569
how I can reach her, please tell me.

24:07.612 --> 24:09.531
Now that your contract's inactive,

24:09.614 --> 24:12.617
I can't give you more details
regarding Noh In-ji, I'm afraid.

24:12.701 --> 24:13.702
Sorry about that.

24:15.370 --> 24:17.372
[pensive piano music playing]

24:18.081 --> 24:19.124
[disconnect tone]

24:28.508 --> 24:30.510
[pensive piano music continues]

24:34.556 --> 24:38.226
Well, he isn't suing us.
No case for breach of contract, no fines.

24:38.310 --> 24:39.519
That's a relief.

24:39.603 --> 24:41.855
Look, I need you to protect Jeong-won.

24:43.356 --> 24:47.402
Even if it's not… in NM's interest
to take those kinds of precautions.

24:49.029 --> 24:50.530
It's strange, you doing this.

24:51.031 --> 24:54.534
The contract's done for you two.
You're both taking care of each other.

24:58.663 --> 24:59.581
Goodbye.

25:01.333 --> 25:03.376
Around two years into my own marriage,

25:04.711 --> 25:06.588
I almost ended up killing my husband.

25:11.301 --> 25:12.302
When it's good,

25:13.220 --> 25:15.263
marriage is a transaction, In-ji.

25:18.808 --> 25:22.103
Do you think you are… really in love?

25:24.648 --> 25:25.649
Are you scared?

25:27.192 --> 25:29.027
Enough to terminate your marriage?

25:53.718 --> 25:56.471
[Ji-o] Nice to see you here.
Feels like we're coworkers.

25:56.972 --> 26:00.100
Welcome to the sad little soiree
of spurned exes and rejects.

26:03.311 --> 26:04.938
I happened to like my marriage.

26:05.689 --> 26:08.692
Now, thanks to you, there's a stain
on my otherwise stellar record.

26:08.775 --> 26:11.152
And also, I'm in trouble
with the company's COO.

26:13.405 --> 26:14.656
[phone buzzing]

26:19.578 --> 26:21.580
[unsettling music playing]

26:34.134 --> 26:37.846
[Tae-seong] Hello? Finally! Why would you
leave your phone off like that?

26:40.515 --> 26:43.768
This thing's hard to open.
Harder than I thought.

26:43.852 --> 26:45.687
It's got a double lock,

26:46.438 --> 26:48.315
which means two sets of combinations.

26:48.398 --> 26:49.983
Just some extra security.

26:50.066 --> 26:52.193
[chuckles] It's nice, huh?

26:53.528 --> 26:54.654
The trunk, I mean.

26:55.280 --> 26:56.656
I've got it right here.

26:57.657 --> 26:59.743
Just can't open the fucking thing.

27:01.161 --> 27:02.329
You mean you just…

27:04.456 --> 27:06.207
Tae-seong, did you steal the trunk?

27:06.958 --> 27:08.752
Hmm, I guess I did.

27:09.711 --> 27:11.212
But now what do I do?

27:12.922 --> 27:15.091
Should I take the contract
you're hiding inside of it

27:15.175 --> 27:16.593
and reveal it to the whole world?

27:18.887 --> 27:20.680
Or should I kill Jeong-won first?

27:21.306 --> 27:22.849
Two options. Come on, pick.

27:24.351 --> 27:25.852
That contract is done now.

27:26.603 --> 27:28.938
Listen, I'm not involved with him.
It's completely over.

27:29.439 --> 27:30.315
How come?

27:30.982 --> 27:31.983
Because of me?

27:32.776 --> 27:33.777
[chuckles softly]

27:36.988 --> 27:39.366
I'll take care of Jeong-won. Okay, In-ji?

27:41.451 --> 27:43.703
The contract is over. Okay, Tae-seong?

27:43.787 --> 27:44.954
Not yet, it isn't.

27:45.664 --> 27:47.040
This didn't happen before.

27:47.123 --> 27:49.584
I remember you
with those men you didn't love.

27:49.668 --> 27:52.212
It was good for us.
Now you don't care at all!

27:52.295 --> 27:53.380
[breathes deeply]

27:53.463 --> 27:54.714
I can't stand Jeong-won

27:54.798 --> 27:58.426
and those damn suits you work for
at that company. They did this to me!

27:59.427 --> 28:02.347
NM's trying to get me committed
to a mental hospital again.

28:02.430 --> 28:05.600
Maybe they'll try to off me this time.
Who knows? Huh?

28:05.684 --> 28:06.601
[chuckles]

28:07.310 --> 28:08.603
Since it's come to this,

28:09.688 --> 28:12.691
I will need a backup plan. Ya know?

28:13.733 --> 28:16.486
Please. I'll… I'll unlock it for you.

28:17.070 --> 28:18.571
[sighs]

28:21.658 --> 28:23.243
I'm in. Where should we meet?

28:24.577 --> 28:26.579
[unsettling music continues]

28:28.164 --> 28:29.207
[disconnect tone]

28:44.973 --> 28:46.975
[unsettling music continues]

28:55.233 --> 28:57.068
[Ji-o] Seo-yeon. Seo-yeon.

28:57.152 --> 28:59.612
Seo-yeon! Seo-yeon, wake up!

29:01.406 --> 29:04.743
Let's do a gastric lavage.
Full blood panel. And call the cops.

29:05.577 --> 29:06.828
Hey, wake up, Seo-yeon.

29:07.328 --> 29:10.331
You need to wake up, Seo-yeon!
Come on, Seo-yeon.

29:11.332 --> 29:12.917
[music fades]

29:18.757 --> 29:20.425
[Ji-o] I guess it's come to this.

29:22.761 --> 29:23.970
Is this what you wanted?

29:27.515 --> 29:30.101
She's always been kinda unhinged,
you know?

29:33.646 --> 29:35.315
She said she wants to live with you.

29:40.111 --> 29:41.571
Well, that's crazy.

29:41.654 --> 29:43.364
You know what will
happen to her, Jeong-won?

29:43.448 --> 29:45.325
She will OD just to prove a point to us.

29:48.286 --> 29:49.662
Can you live with that?

29:55.251 --> 29:57.253
[melancholy music playing]

30:05.720 --> 30:08.097
My guess is I can't persuade you, so…

30:10.767 --> 30:13.144
so go through with it
if that's what you want.

30:14.646 --> 30:15.730
Sorry, Ji-o.

30:20.068 --> 30:22.862
And don't call me. I'll be busy today.

30:43.925 --> 30:45.552
[car engine starts]

30:55.270 --> 30:56.104
[glass clinks]

30:58.982 --> 31:00.483
[music fades]

31:00.567 --> 31:02.235
I thought I would be comfortable.

31:03.027 --> 31:04.362
Take the room down here.

31:10.368 --> 31:12.370
Acting like a little boy
is gonna wear you down.

31:12.453 --> 31:13.538
We're even now, aren't we?

31:14.622 --> 31:16.457
[pants]

31:18.418 --> 31:21.921
Look, I let you into my house again
'cause I wanted to give you a second.

31:23.256 --> 31:25.550
A second to accept the hard truth.

31:25.633 --> 31:28.094
I've always wondered why
I couldn't bring myself to leave you.

31:28.177 --> 31:30.638
I realized it's because I pitied you.

31:33.057 --> 31:34.392
Seo-yeon, listen.

31:35.101 --> 31:37.020
There is no going back for us.

31:38.104 --> 31:39.314
Neither one of us.

31:49.407 --> 31:50.658
[door opens]

31:51.826 --> 31:52.869
[door closes]

32:02.962 --> 32:05.006
[glass shatters]

32:05.089 --> 32:07.425
[breathing heavily]

32:09.302 --> 32:11.304
[stirring music playing]

32:13.598 --> 32:16.851
[Si-jeong] Wait. Are you seriously going?
What are you gonna do by yourself?

32:16.935 --> 32:19.103
I'll head over right now.
Tell me where you are.

32:20.772 --> 32:24.359
Si-jeong… I think
I have screwed up everything.

32:25.693 --> 32:26.611
You're saying…

32:27.654 --> 32:29.530
Maybe it's all my fault. All of it.

32:31.032 --> 32:33.618
Hye-yeong. Do-ha too.

32:34.827 --> 32:35.870
And Jeong-won.

32:36.955 --> 32:39.749
[groans] What the hell?
Come on! That makes no sense!

32:40.833 --> 32:43.002
Hey, In-ji! Oh, come on!

32:43.086 --> 32:44.796
In-ji, hey! Don't say that!

32:44.879 --> 32:45.922
[disconnect tone]

32:55.473 --> 32:56.808
[phone line ringing]

33:00.478 --> 33:02.438
NOH IN-JI

33:04.565 --> 33:07.402
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed cannot be reached.

33:07.485 --> 33:08.820
At the tone--

33:09.904 --> 33:11.781
NOH IN-JI

33:11.864 --> 33:13.199
[phone buzzing]

33:13.992 --> 33:15.493
[phone buzzing]

33:15.576 --> 33:17.495
HAN JEONG-WON

33:17.578 --> 33:19.580
[uneasy music playing]

33:26.379 --> 33:28.381
[grass rustling]

33:54.157 --> 33:55.324
[trunk clatters]

33:57.326 --> 33:59.746
All alone tonight? You're brave, huh?

34:00.872 --> 34:02.498
Should I be afraid right now, Tae-seong?

34:02.582 --> 34:04.333
No. Not you, lovely In-ji.

34:06.085 --> 34:08.713
- All right, I'll open it up for you.
- Whoa, slow down.

34:08.796 --> 34:11.257
Hey, come on. What's the hurry?
I mean, we just got here.

34:14.886 --> 34:17.597
Okay. So the contract and the manual,
it's all in here?

34:18.306 --> 34:19.140
It's evidence.

34:26.689 --> 34:28.274
What's with that look? Are you afraid

34:28.983 --> 34:31.569
if you say the combination,
you'll end up like Do-ha?

34:31.652 --> 34:34.197
You're afraid people will
point fingers at you?

34:34.864 --> 34:38.826
You seem kinda excited that I might
get into serious trouble, Tae-seong.

34:39.911 --> 34:42.830
Honestly, making it official
is the best-case scenario anyway.

34:42.914 --> 34:45.041
Then I'll be the only thing you have left.

34:46.000 --> 34:47.126
[Tae-seong chuckles]

34:51.464 --> 34:54.634
You saw it back then… with Do-ha.

34:55.259 --> 34:57.637
How would it benefit you?
Think about this.

34:58.679 --> 35:01.224
Being stuck to my side,
sharing my suffering.

35:05.603 --> 35:07.563
There's still time to turn this around.

35:08.272 --> 35:10.399
Just go move on with your life, Tae-seong.

35:11.150 --> 35:14.070
Just leave me be,
and I swear I'll forget all about this.

35:14.570 --> 35:15.571
The thing is…

35:17.573 --> 35:19.492
I won't suffer like you.

35:21.327 --> 35:23.663
I mean, what do I care if you're miserable

35:23.746 --> 35:27.250
and your life is in shambles as long as
you stay with me forever, In-ji?

35:30.002 --> 35:31.963
Sounds like a good life.

35:33.506 --> 35:34.799
[chuckles]

35:37.885 --> 35:39.846
I killed this pharmacist not too long ago.

35:39.929 --> 35:42.515
Pretty sure I told you about that.
You remember I killed a person?

35:43.683 --> 35:45.685
Turns out it's a lot easier
than I thought.

35:46.269 --> 35:49.689
As for the cops,
they still have no idea who did it.

35:49.772 --> 35:51.274
[chuckles]

35:52.358 --> 35:54.819
[unsettling music playing]

35:59.365 --> 36:00.449
[tires squeal]

36:04.287 --> 36:08.124
[Tae-seong] I'm night-kayaking
with Ms. Noh right now. Care to join us?

36:09.333 --> 36:10.501
Crazy ass.

36:11.085 --> 36:12.044
NOH IN-JI

36:12.837 --> 36:14.046
[phone line ringing]

36:15.047 --> 36:17.884
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed cannot be reached.

36:17.967 --> 36:19.260
[disconnect tone]

36:22.388 --> 36:24.140
- [tires squeal]
- [engine roars]

36:26.058 --> 36:28.477
[unsettling music continues]

36:38.738 --> 36:39.906
What's wrong?

36:41.199 --> 36:43.951
Where did…
where did you find this, Tae-seong?

36:44.035 --> 36:45.995
Where do you think?
Jeong-won's house. The closet.

36:46.829 --> 36:47.705
In his room.

36:50.958 --> 36:52.418
[eerie music sting]

36:57.215 --> 36:58.549
[unsettling music resumes]

36:59.592 --> 37:00.843
[Tae-seong] What's the problem?

37:03.888 --> 37:06.265
Well, I don't know.
It looks like the lock is jammed

37:06.349 --> 37:08.809
because, uh,
you tried to break it off first.

37:10.937 --> 37:13.064
Oh, give me a fucking break.

37:15.066 --> 37:18.194
You have got to be fucking kidding me!
Jesus Christ!

37:19.987 --> 37:23.574
Tomorrow we can just take it into a store.
They'll take care of it for us.

37:26.535 --> 37:28.454
In-ji, do you think I'm a fool? Huh?!

37:28.537 --> 37:30.539
[breathing nervously]

37:31.540 --> 37:33.376
Come on. What the hell do you want?

37:33.876 --> 37:35.711
You could've brought it to me right away.

37:35.795 --> 37:39.465
And you should've brought it right to me,
but you busted it like an idiot!

37:42.843 --> 37:44.887
[yells] God-fucking-damn it!

37:44.971 --> 37:46.138
[grunts]

37:49.517 --> 37:50.518
Oh shit!

37:51.310 --> 37:52.645
[grunting]

37:53.187 --> 37:54.689
[straining] Open up!

37:55.231 --> 37:56.732
[grunts] Fucking thing!

37:56.816 --> 37:57.817
Fuck!

38:04.907 --> 38:07.827
Will you stop with the manic nonsense
if I'm dead and gone?

38:14.125 --> 38:15.293
Eom Tae-seong, let's…

38:17.295 --> 38:19.213
let's die together, the two of us.

38:21.507 --> 38:23.426
Come on. That's a nice idea, right?

38:25.052 --> 38:27.054
[sighs]

38:29.181 --> 38:30.349
Well, holy shit.

38:31.267 --> 38:34.937
You've been working on your jokes.
You really had me for a second.

38:35.813 --> 38:37.148
[Tae-seong chuckles]

38:37.231 --> 38:39.817
Hmm, but we can't die tonight.

38:42.903 --> 38:44.655
Option number two is good.

38:44.739 --> 38:45.948
[stirring music playing]

38:46.032 --> 38:47.033
Number two?

38:48.159 --> 38:50.161
[stirring music continues]

39:01.422 --> 39:03.466
[car door opens and closes]

39:03.549 --> 39:05.551
[stirring electronic music playing]

39:07.053 --> 39:09.472
Hey, In-ji? In-ji!

39:10.681 --> 39:11.807
You know,

39:12.850 --> 39:15.644
if I were to kill someone,
I'd just go back to the hospital.

39:16.145 --> 39:17.229
[Jeong-won] Can you hear me?

39:17.730 --> 39:20.274
Why are you doing this?
God, what the hell is wrong with you?

39:20.358 --> 39:21.400
[Jeong-won] In-ji!

39:21.484 --> 39:22.693
Just because.

39:22.777 --> 39:24.945
- There's no reason in particular.
- In-ji, where are you?

39:26.072 --> 39:28.240
- [Jeong-won] In-ji, hang on!
- [In-ji breathing nervously]

39:28.324 --> 39:30.284
Sh!

39:31.827 --> 39:33.871
In-ji, are… are you all right?

39:33.954 --> 39:35.748
Stay back, Jeong-won. Just stay back.

39:35.831 --> 39:36.707
[grunts]

39:36.791 --> 39:38.834
[In-ji panting]

39:42.630 --> 39:43.714
[In-ji screams]

39:44.423 --> 39:46.926
[grunting]

39:47.676 --> 39:48.719
[Tae-seong] Die.

39:48.803 --> 39:50.429
[all grunting]

39:51.597 --> 39:53.432
[music swells]

39:53.516 --> 39:55.518
[breathing nervously]

40:05.069 --> 40:07.071
[stirring music playing]

40:11.242 --> 40:12.785
[both panting]

40:12.868 --> 40:14.286
[In-ji grunts]

40:14.370 --> 40:16.372
[both panting]

40:20.292 --> 40:22.294
[In-ji breathing frantically]

40:31.011 --> 40:32.054
[Tae-seong grunts]

40:34.306 --> 40:36.058
[In-ji breathing heavily]

40:36.142 --> 40:37.143
[In-ji screams]

40:37.226 --> 40:39.437
[both panting]

40:39.520 --> 40:42.273
It's over. It's over.
You're gonna be okay.

40:42.356 --> 40:43.566
I shot Tae-seong.

40:44.108 --> 40:47.111
I did. I swear I… I shot…

40:47.736 --> 40:51.907
[exhales sharply] It's okay.
What matters is you're safe.

40:53.117 --> 40:54.160
I shot…

40:54.994 --> 40:56.203
[In-ji whimpers]

40:56.871 --> 40:58.205
[panting]

41:00.499 --> 41:01.917
[In-ji sobs]

41:03.836 --> 41:06.755
[In-ji panting, sobbing]

41:09.925 --> 41:11.927
[both breathing heavily]

41:14.388 --> 41:16.390
[In-ji panting]

41:19.852 --> 41:20.978
[Jeong-won] It's okay.

41:21.520 --> 41:23.939
[stirring music continues]

41:30.738 --> 41:32.156
[engine starts]

41:44.126 --> 41:45.544
[music fades]

42:12.071 --> 42:13.948
Weren't there live rounds in the gun?

42:24.792 --> 42:28.128
I thought I'd kill myself
if I left it loaded, and…

42:33.050 --> 42:34.468
and I guess I should have.

42:37.972 --> 42:39.557
I should've killed him myself.

42:41.684 --> 42:43.561
[wistful music playing]

42:43.644 --> 42:44.979
You had no reason.

42:45.479 --> 42:46.730
It's my issue, not yours.

42:50.985 --> 42:53.862
I did not put myself
in the middle of this for you.

42:54.530 --> 42:56.031
That's just not the case.

42:58.534 --> 43:01.078
I can keep both of us safe. We'll be fine.

43:02.454 --> 43:03.539
Glad to hear it.

43:05.082 --> 43:07.668
Keep yourself safe, then, Jeong-won.
Go right ahead.

43:09.753 --> 43:11.672
And I can handle the rest, all right?

43:12.256 --> 43:13.215
In-ji…

43:15.050 --> 43:16.468
[sighs]

43:17.886 --> 43:19.555
I just want this to be over.

43:23.559 --> 43:24.393
I'm…

43:26.437 --> 43:28.063
so tired of all of it.

43:43.871 --> 43:45.873
[wistful music continues]

43:56.800 --> 43:57.635
[sighs]

44:20.366 --> 44:21.992
[man inhales deeply]

44:22.076 --> 44:25.788
So they were blanks,
and you fired in self-defense?

44:25.871 --> 44:27.164
[music fades]

44:27.247 --> 44:28.791
Well, despite that fact,

44:28.874 --> 44:31.627
you'll still be charged
for the possession of an illegal weapon.

44:31.710 --> 44:32.836
Understand?

44:35.214 --> 44:36.048
Yes.

44:39.385 --> 44:40.386
[groans]

44:45.557 --> 44:46.809
So tell me,

44:47.601 --> 44:49.478
who do you think killed Tae-seong?

44:50.187 --> 44:52.189
[unsettling music playing]

45:06.912 --> 45:08.914
[unsettling music continues]

45:10.290 --> 45:12.918
[engine sputtering]

45:14.086 --> 45:16.088
[engine sputtering]

45:17.172 --> 45:18.173
Shit.

45:19.717 --> 45:21.343
[grunts]

45:21.427 --> 45:23.679
[grunting continues]

45:24.763 --> 45:26.765
[gasps, groans]

45:28.267 --> 45:29.601
[screams]

45:30.144 --> 45:32.354
[breathing frantically]

45:32.438 --> 45:34.440
[tense music playing]

45:34.523 --> 45:36.525
[boat approaching]

45:43.699 --> 45:45.701
[music intensifies]

45:50.706 --> 45:52.040
[blade slices]

45:52.124 --> 45:54.418
[tense music continues]

45:57.004 --> 45:58.964
[tense music swells]

45:59.047 --> 46:00.758
[unsettling music playing]

46:23.906 --> 46:25.574
[Seon] I can't help but think

46:25.657 --> 46:27.951
you're the ideal choice
for this task, Ji-o.

46:31.914 --> 46:35.250
Eom Tae-seong.
Think you can take care of it for us?

46:36.084 --> 46:38.086
[unsettling music continues]

46:49.890 --> 46:51.016
[door opens]

46:52.267 --> 46:53.352
[door closes]

46:55.896 --> 46:57.898
[music subsides]

47:01.485 --> 47:03.654
I admit I've been wrong about all of this.

47:04.655 --> 47:06.281
I think you are the one I need.

47:07.574 --> 47:09.117
I'm saying you finally won.

47:29.263 --> 47:31.098
[uneasy music playing]

47:31.181 --> 47:32.766
The blade's not usually like this, right?

47:34.935 --> 47:36.103
Uh…

47:37.396 --> 47:38.981
What have you been up to, Ji-o?

47:41.525 --> 47:42.776
I'm afraid I…

47:46.655 --> 47:48.115
killed someone earlier.

47:53.078 --> 47:54.746
I was a guard for NM.

47:55.497 --> 47:57.666
[uneasy music continues]

48:01.753 --> 48:05.382
I was there when Tae-seong killed
that other keeper years ago…

48:07.259 --> 48:08.468
but I ran away.

48:08.552 --> 48:09.761
[music fades]

48:09.845 --> 48:12.598
That stuck with me,
and it's been bothering me ever since.

48:15.350 --> 48:17.436
But that wasn't the only reason I did it.

48:27.696 --> 48:29.448
I liked being married to you.

48:31.533 --> 48:33.827
[wistful music playing]

48:35.787 --> 48:37.539
I'll move out soon and leave you alone.

48:58.936 --> 49:00.938
[wistful music continues]

49:05.734 --> 49:09.780
[man] So why is it that Eom Tae-seong had
your trunk in his possession, Mrs. Lee?

49:10.280 --> 49:11.365
Who knows?

49:11.990 --> 49:14.409
I rarely used that trunk
'cause it was so difficult to unlock.

49:14.993 --> 49:17.079
And that's why you left it at Jeong-won's?

49:17.996 --> 49:19.456
Something like that, I guess.

49:27.255 --> 49:30.425
He was killed with a very long,
pointy weapon that left a precise wound.

49:30.509 --> 49:31.843
There was a single hole.

49:39.101 --> 49:41.269
Now, what kind of sound does that make?

49:42.604 --> 49:44.022
Sounds like a length of rebar.

49:44.106 --> 49:46.608
I've seen those sharpened into stakes
at construction sites.

49:46.692 --> 49:47.693
Uh, no.

49:48.402 --> 49:50.445
Smoother than that.
That would be too dull.

49:52.364 --> 49:53.782
There are lots of things like that.

49:55.200 --> 49:56.368
[music fades]

49:57.619 --> 50:00.664
I don't know why you'd ask me
such a specific question.

50:09.381 --> 50:11.717
If there are no more questions,
can I go now?

50:11.800 --> 50:13.051
I'm really tired.

50:14.803 --> 50:16.888
Well, we've already pored over
the trunk's contents.

50:16.972 --> 50:19.599
You should take a look as well
to make sure everything's still there.

50:19.683 --> 50:21.643
If you say
an item's missing at a later time,

50:21.727 --> 50:23.729
we won't be able to help, that's all.

50:34.322 --> 50:36.324
[stirring music playing]

51:12.778 --> 51:14.780
[stirring music continues]

51:24.206 --> 51:25.332
[door closes]

51:25.415 --> 51:28.710
Hey, so the realtor said that…
it's a buyer's market,

51:28.794 --> 51:30.921
and they had to
lower the price to rent it.

51:33.423 --> 51:36.802
Take good care of these guys.
You've got a great track record with that.

51:38.220 --> 51:40.889
Think about cutting back on
the amount of coffee you drink.

51:41.389 --> 51:43.058
Stop lecturing me.

51:43.141 --> 51:44.392
Take care, okay?

51:48.730 --> 51:49.564
What's wrong?

51:50.357 --> 51:52.818
Will you live happily ever after
with that prick?

51:55.278 --> 51:56.404
What is it?

51:57.531 --> 52:00.075
I hope NM keeps you busy
with another young wife.

52:01.076 --> 52:02.160
[chuckles]

52:03.161 --> 52:05.997
I had a feeling you knew the truth
about me all along, In-ji.

52:06.081 --> 52:07.290
God, you're something else.

52:08.125 --> 52:09.793
[chuckles] You're the worst.

52:10.377 --> 52:12.170
Well, I should've just
come out with it sooner.

52:12.254 --> 52:15.465
To think I spent all that time
beating myself up. Fuck me.

52:16.967 --> 52:18.009
I'll get going.

52:22.973 --> 52:25.100
[Do-dam] "This too shall pass."
Don't forget it.

52:25.976 --> 52:27.686
That's all there is to married life.

52:28.270 --> 52:30.730
You can trust me.
I've been divorced three times.

52:33.733 --> 52:35.735
[sentimental music playing]

52:42.200 --> 52:44.327
[sentimental music continues]

53:11.313 --> 53:12.856
So is that everything you brought?

53:14.107 --> 53:16.318
A trunkload
is all you need for a marriage.

53:26.703 --> 53:29.956
I wonder why it never crossed my mind
to just leave this house.

53:31.625 --> 53:32.667
Was I afraid?

53:33.710 --> 53:34.836
I think you're just lazy.

53:38.173 --> 53:40.425
The thing is, moving requires diligence.

53:41.509 --> 53:43.011
Squabbling with the old landlord,

53:44.012 --> 53:45.847
get a new fridge, a new kitchen table,

53:45.931 --> 53:48.433
not to mention
you have to find the new curtains.

53:52.354 --> 53:54.022
Hey, you are one to talk, you know.

53:55.440 --> 53:57.275
Because if I were you, I would have…

53:58.610 --> 54:00.570
I would've left that flat a while ago.

54:03.031 --> 54:03.865
I doubt that.

54:04.574 --> 54:05.742
[music fades]

54:07.244 --> 54:09.996
So you're…
really gonna tear down this house?

54:10.914 --> 54:11.748
Why?

54:12.832 --> 54:15.669
I guess I'm too soft
to squabble with an old landlord.

54:16.378 --> 54:18.922
I know I'll get tired of something new
and come crawling back here,

54:19.005 --> 54:22.259
so I need to get to the root of this
and just burn it down.

54:36.648 --> 54:38.024
[thud]

54:40.735 --> 54:43.363
You're gonna demolish it anyway. Come on.

54:53.248 --> 54:55.250
[melodic piano music playing]

55:13.476 --> 55:15.895
♪ You don't have to stay ♪

55:15.979 --> 55:18.606
♪ Just let the past decay ♪

55:18.690 --> 55:21.526
♪ 'Cause I know it's not your fault ♪

55:23.570 --> 55:25.655
♪ You think you're not enough… ♪

55:27.657 --> 55:29.284
What were you gonna say to me?

55:30.618 --> 55:32.579
The night you said, "If I were you."

55:33.246 --> 55:34.205
Was this it?

55:34.789 --> 55:36.958
That you wanted me
to get out of this house?

55:39.586 --> 55:41.338
You've been thinking about that?

55:42.339 --> 55:43.798
Is that the reason you're doing this?

55:45.884 --> 55:47.302
So you were not saying that?

55:49.679 --> 55:51.306
I was just talking…

55:56.394 --> 55:57.937
about how you should…

56:00.607 --> 56:01.649
rent it out.

56:04.194 --> 56:06.738
Basically, I was saying
I'd use the money from renting it out

56:06.821 --> 56:08.448
to travel if I owned the house.

56:09.199 --> 56:10.950
I didn't think you'd do
something like this.

56:12.369 --> 56:14.788
Ah, renting it out.

56:16.956 --> 56:18.541
♪ Mm-mm ♪

56:18.625 --> 56:21.753
♪ What do we live for… ♪

56:23.380 --> 56:25.215
Do you think you might stay with me…

56:28.593 --> 56:30.345
if we see each other down the road?

56:32.639 --> 56:36.142
Who knows?
We could… be destined to be together.

56:37.769 --> 56:39.229
I mean, probably not forever.

56:40.146 --> 56:41.940
I could do, like, three decades.

56:43.525 --> 56:44.567
[In-ji chuckles]

56:48.446 --> 56:50.657
And what if we run into each other
two times in a row?

56:50.740 --> 56:53.910
♪ Calling you again and again… ♪

56:54.702 --> 56:56.913
Look, if it happens twice,
that's providence.

56:57.831 --> 57:00.375
♪ All the clouds and storms before us… ♪

57:00.458 --> 57:01.584
So two times.

57:03.336 --> 57:04.546
Would it do?

57:05.130 --> 57:07.090
♪ Turn around ♪

57:07.173 --> 57:08.425
♪ Oh ♪

57:08.508 --> 57:12.262
♪ Baby, I'll be your savior… ♪

57:12.929 --> 57:14.931
I'm grateful for everything you've done.

57:17.267 --> 57:19.352
♪ What if we die… ♪

57:20.728 --> 57:23.606
I need you to know that
no matter what the future brings.

57:27.485 --> 57:29.320
♪ What if we try ♪

57:29.946 --> 57:31.281
♪ To stay alive? ♪

57:31.364 --> 57:34.951
♪ Will we ever be free from the past? ♪

57:35.034 --> 57:37.954
♪ You know I am your savior ♪

57:38.037 --> 57:40.248
♪ Holding you so close… ♪

57:44.294 --> 57:46.296
[music ends]

58:11.196 --> 58:15.825
DEAD BODY DISCOVERED AT LAKE
MURDER SUSPECT TAKEN INTO CUSTODY

58:15.909 --> 58:18.912
- [stirring music playing]
- [reporters clamoring]

58:20.955 --> 58:22.957
[camera shutters clicking]

58:30.965 --> 58:31.966
[connect tone]

58:32.050 --> 58:33.176
[phone line ringing]

58:36.221 --> 58:38.306
Hi. Mr. Choi, listen.

58:39.432 --> 58:40.767
I think I have a case for you.

58:55.615 --> 58:58.618
Yoon-a asked me to check in
on the remodel. That's why I'm here.

58:58.701 --> 59:00.703
You don't need to explain yourself.

59:00.787 --> 59:03.998
I know, but… I can't help it.
You know that.

59:04.499 --> 59:05.833
[music fades]

59:07.502 --> 59:09.629
Ji-o and I are renewing our contract.

59:10.129 --> 59:12.340
And I'm hiring a top-notch lawyer.

59:17.679 --> 59:18.596
Seo-yeon.

59:22.100 --> 59:24.394
I thought I was being suffocated,
and it was your fault.

59:25.979 --> 59:27.313
But now I think I was

59:29.107 --> 59:30.858
holding you back from what you wanted.

59:32.193 --> 59:34.487
I never explained
why things weren't working.

59:34.571 --> 59:36.155
I should've been honest.

59:39.242 --> 59:40.451
Well, I was the villain.

59:41.494 --> 59:43.329
That's how I got my closure with you.

59:44.497 --> 59:46.499
It hurts my pride less to think that.

59:58.720 --> 01:00:01.139
[melodic acoustic guitar music playing]

01:00:15.320 --> 01:00:17.405
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

01:00:28.166 --> 01:00:30.543
Momo. Hey, Mo. Momo.

01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:32.712
You're sleepy, huh?

01:00:32.795 --> 01:00:33.963
[chuckles]

01:00:34.839 --> 01:00:36.424
Hey, Cookie.

01:00:36.507 --> 01:00:38.593
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

01:01:25.973 --> 01:01:27.141
[sighs]

01:01:30.311 --> 01:01:31.521
Yeah, I'm lonely.

01:01:34.565 --> 01:01:36.651
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

01:01:53.376 --> 01:01:59.716
ITERATION

01:02:02.301 --> 01:02:04.303
[melodic acoustic guitar music continues]

01:02:04.387 --> 01:02:06.472
[woman in film breathing heavily]

01:02:10.184 --> 01:02:11.602
[screams]

01:02:11.686 --> 01:02:12.895
[panting fearfully]

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:20.903
DIRECTED BY NOH SU-HWAN
SCREENPLAY BY YANG JEONG-WON

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:30.580
MUSIC BY HAN JEONG-WON

01:02:35.334 --> 01:02:36.794
[music fades]

01:02:41.674 --> 01:02:42.842
[phone buzzes]

01:02:46.763 --> 01:02:47.889
[phone buzzes]

01:02:56.397 --> 01:02:57.440
What?

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.524
[Hyeon-cheol] Hey, man.

01:02:58.608 --> 01:03:01.152
So the film finally got released.
Only ten months late.

01:03:01.235 --> 01:03:02.487
The reviews are lukewarm.

01:03:03.279 --> 01:03:04.113
Makes sense.

01:03:04.197 --> 01:03:07.825
Does anyone actually go to the theater
to watch B-horror movies nowadays?

01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:11.204
I know you're not fishing,
so stop moping around, will you?

01:03:11.287 --> 01:03:13.289
- Come back to work.
- I'm not at the lake.

01:03:13.790 --> 01:03:16.834
Get back here, dude.
I think my wife's leaving me.

01:03:18.252 --> 01:03:19.253
Not as bad as you think.

01:03:20.713 --> 01:03:21.672
[disconnect tone]

01:03:27.637 --> 01:03:30.014
- [Hyeon-cheol] What is this again?
- [Yoon-a] Divorce papers.

01:03:30.681 --> 01:03:32.809
I've been filling them out
a little every day.

01:03:32.892 --> 01:03:33.726
Why's that?

01:03:33.810 --> 01:03:36.938
The only way I can get any space is taking
you and the kids out of the equation.

01:03:37.021 --> 01:03:38.147
How do you not have space?

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:41.234
I gave you exclusive rights
to the bathroom 'cause you're constipated.

01:03:42.068 --> 01:03:43.361
You think I have space?

01:03:43.444 --> 01:03:46.072
You've got a name, right?
Oh Hyeon-cheol. You have a job, don't you?

01:03:46.697 --> 01:03:49.283
What about me? I have nothing.
I'm just a mother and your wife.

01:03:49.367 --> 01:03:51.744
You have a nice office
with a plaque and a big desk.

01:03:52.245 --> 01:03:55.957
I have a big circle of friends,
and no one else is married, you know that?

01:03:56.040 --> 01:03:57.625
They're all happy, doing amazing things.

01:03:57.708 --> 01:04:00.586
Meanwhile, I've accomplished nothing.
I don't know where my life's going.

01:04:01.379 --> 01:04:02.338
And I get it, okay?

01:04:02.421 --> 01:04:05.383
Someone has to raise the kids
and take care of them. I know that.

01:04:06.425 --> 01:04:07.844
[breathes heavily]

01:04:08.845 --> 01:04:10.012
I just-- I…

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:12.932
[sobs]

01:04:14.642 --> 01:04:18.187
I just don't think that I'm happy
with that choice at all, and…

01:04:18.771 --> 01:04:19.856
[crying]

01:04:20.940 --> 01:04:21.941
[sighs]

01:04:22.733 --> 01:04:26.529
Maybe you should get a laser treatment.
I'll give you a card.

01:04:26.612 --> 01:04:27.655
Mine, not the company card.

01:04:27.738 --> 01:04:30.324
Why can't we even have
a serious conversation?

01:04:30.992 --> 01:04:33.035
Are you not capable of that?!

01:04:33.536 --> 01:04:35.997
Wow. Just 3,000?

01:04:36.706 --> 01:04:38.833
I can give you a lot more, you know.

01:04:38.916 --> 01:04:40.668
That's all right. That amount's fine.

01:04:41.168 --> 01:04:44.255
A little odd
to turn down a better offer, hmm? [laughs]

01:04:44.964 --> 01:04:46.257
No dead bodies in here, right?

01:04:47.341 --> 01:04:48.217
[woman cackles]

01:04:48.301 --> 01:04:49.969
Just kidding. Here ya go.

01:04:50.052 --> 01:04:51.304
[woman laughs]

01:04:51.387 --> 01:04:52.680
- Thank you.
- Have a nice day.

01:04:52.763 --> 01:04:54.765
[woman] Oh yeah. You bet. I always do.

01:04:55.349 --> 01:04:57.602
What a beauty. My gosh. Mm!

01:04:58.144 --> 01:04:59.312
[woman hisses]

01:04:59.395 --> 01:05:02.023
What am I gonna do with you, huh?

01:05:02.982 --> 01:05:05.359
What an incredible design. Mm.

01:05:05.443 --> 01:05:06.527
[woman laughs]

01:05:18.205 --> 01:05:20.958
AMERICANO 3,000 WON

01:05:29.216 --> 01:05:30.801
[woman] Thanks so much. Enjoy.

01:05:30.885 --> 01:05:32.136
[In-ji] Have a nice day.

01:05:49.528 --> 01:05:51.530
[romantic pop music playing]

01:07:25.374 --> 01:07:27.376
[romantic pop music continues]

01:07:44.143 --> 01:07:47.646
Uh… I was just taking my cat
over to the vet.

01:07:48.773 --> 01:07:50.608
One of his paws was a bit sore, and…

01:07:52.151 --> 01:07:54.653
Oh, right. I do have a…
I do have a few cats now.

01:07:56.113 --> 01:07:56.947
Oh.

01:08:00.201 --> 01:08:01.619
Everything going okay?

01:08:05.915 --> 01:08:07.416
It was pretty scary.

01:08:09.710 --> 01:08:11.462
I saw your movie.

01:08:14.256 --> 01:08:16.050
You see the credits, by any chance?

01:08:18.219 --> 01:08:19.887
That's the whole reason I went.

01:08:29.897 --> 01:08:31.190
It's number one, In-ji.

01:08:34.568 --> 01:08:36.237
Our first chance encounter.

01:08:45.162 --> 01:08:47.123
One more to go before we get it right.

01:08:49.667 --> 01:08:50.501
Yeah.

01:08:53.754 --> 01:08:55.756
[romantic pop music continues]

01:09:13.065 --> 01:09:15.067
[romantic pop music continues]

01:11:12.434 --> 01:11:14.728
[music fades]
